1
00:00:00,048 --> 00:00:02,889
So I have this deployment.md file in this

2
00:00:03,001 --> 00:00:05,858
demo project I provided and in there I have

3
00:00:05,970 --> 00:00:07,992
the deployment steps we need to go through.

4
00:00:08,923 --> 00:00:10,705
What gets deployed as I mentioned is this

5
00:00:10,705 --> 00:00:13,770
Traefik reverse proxy and our web app where

6
00:00:13,819 --> 00:00:17,317
I was using the TanStack Start React Node.js

7
00:00:17,350 --> 00:00:19,532
framework in case you're interested in that.

8
00:00:20,576 --> 00:00:22,726
Now we will need to set up some environment

9
00:00:22,726 --> 00:00:23,192
variables

10
00:00:23,850 --> 00:00:25,198
on our VPS then

11
00:00:26,660 --> 00:00:30,161
to make our Traefik reverse proxy aware of

12
00:00:30,194 --> 00:00:32,301
the domain that will be pointing at that

13
00:00:32,301 --> 00:00:34,829
server. That is important for requesting a

14
00:00:34,829 --> 00:00:37,357
certificate because the certificate is bound

15
00:00:37,406 --> 00:00:39,499
to a certain domain. So we need to tell

16
00:00:39,628 --> 00:00:41,915
Traefik which domain we'll be using so that

17
00:00:41,915 --> 00:00:44,494
it can request and handle the right

18
00:00:44,575 --> 00:00:45,529
certificate for us.

19
00:00:46,078 --> 00:00:48,164
And we'll also need to provide a valid

20
00:00:48,261 --> 00:00:50,185
email, which can be from a different domain,

21
00:00:50,298 --> 00:00:52,577
but it must be a valid email because Let's

22
00:00:52,658 --> 00:00:54,561
Encrypt requires that for issuing a

23
00:00:54,611 --> 00:00:55,327
certificate so that they could, for example,

24
00:00:55,393 --> 00:00:55,992
message us

25
00:00:57,676 --> 00:00:59,824
us if something's wrong with the certificate

26
00:01:00,240 --> 00:01:02,597
or it's about to expire or anything like

27
00:01:02,597 --> 00:01:02,869
that.

28
00:01:04,023 --> 00:01:06,588
But before we do that, we actually wanna get

29
00:01:06,588 --> 00:01:09,778
the project onto the VPS and for that, we

30
00:01:09,778 --> 00:01:11,365
have different options.

31
00:01:12,358 --> 00:01:15,292
We can copy files from our local machine

32
00:01:15,885 --> 00:01:17,632
because this project right now is on my

33
00:01:17,648 --> 00:01:19,764
local MacBook and for you, it's probably on

34
00:01:19,876 --> 00:01:21,799
your laptop or your Windows machine or

35
00:01:21,799 --> 00:01:24,332
whatever. We have to copy that from our

36
00:01:24,540 --> 00:01:28,456
machine to the VPS, so onto the VPS here to

37
00:01:28,472 --> 00:01:30,847
which we are connected via our terminal as

38
00:01:30,943 --> 00:01:32,243
you saw before in the course.

39
00:01:32,950 --> 00:01:35,453
And one tool we can use for this is SCP,

40
00:01:35,614 --> 00:01:37,347
which is a command that should be available

41
00:01:37,459 --> 00:01:40,589
by default on macOS and modern versions of

42
00:01:40,589 --> 00:01:40,958
Windows.

43
00:01:41,536 --> 00:01:44,409
On Windows, you could also use the WSL2

44
00:01:44,682 --> 00:01:47,121
environment and spin up a terminal in there.

45
00:01:47,490 --> 00:01:50,588
And SCP is simply the SSH

46
00:01:51,326 --> 00:01:53,698
copy command in the end to copy a file

47
00:01:53,842 --> 00:01:55,396
across SSH.

48
00:01:55,973 --> 00:01:58,040
And SSH of course was the protocol we used

49
00:01:58,056 --> 00:02:00,444
for connecting to our server. So that simply

50
00:02:00,492 --> 00:02:02,527
is a command we can use for copying files

51
00:02:02,704 --> 00:02:03,729
over SSH.

52
00:02:04,322 --> 00:02:06,213
And if we wanted to use this here, we could

53
00:02:06,325 --> 00:02:08,745
open a terminal in this project on our

54
00:02:08,745 --> 00:02:10,828
machine. Here I'm using the one integrated

55
00:02:10,892 --> 00:02:12,863
in Visual Studio Code, but you can use any

56
00:02:12,895 --> 00:02:15,443
terminal of course. And then simply use the

57
00:02:15,523 --> 00:02:18,653
SCP command here and then dot to point at

58
00:02:18,653 --> 00:02:20,437
the folder in which we are, which is the

59
00:02:20,437 --> 00:02:21,963
overall project folder here for me.

60
00:02:22,927 --> 00:02:23,441
And then

61
00:02:24,197 --> 00:02:25,193
as is also mentioned here,

62
00:02:25,803 --> 00:02:26,655
point at our

63
00:02:27,571 --> 00:02:30,238
remote host and then separated by a colon,

64
00:02:30,302 --> 00:02:33,018
the path on that host where we wanna copy

65
00:02:33,066 --> 00:02:33,629
the app to.

66
00:02:34,271 --> 00:02:37,131
So of course I gave my host an alias earlier

67
00:02:37,147 --> 00:02:39,445
in the course, it's vps-course,

68
00:02:40,120 --> 00:02:42,675
the alias we set up in that SSH config file.

69
00:02:43,493 --> 00:02:43,862
And then

70
00:02:44,520 --> 00:02:47,633
the path separated by a colon could be the

71
00:02:47,729 --> 00:02:49,574
root path of the user

72
00:02:50,376 --> 00:02:52,991
we're connecting with, so the max user in my

73
00:02:53,039 --> 00:02:55,542
case, and then any nested path of your

74
00:02:55,606 --> 00:02:57,997
choice, or you copy it directly into this

75
00:02:57,997 --> 00:03:00,163
path. And you will also need to add the

76
00:03:00,724 --> 00:03:01,735
-r flag here

77
00:03:02,265 --> 00:03:04,190
to make sure that this is copied

78
00:03:04,190 --> 00:03:06,340
recursively, which you need to specify if

79
00:03:06,340 --> 00:03:09,323
you're targeting a folder, and this is It's

80
00:03:09,323 --> 00:03:10,205
my project folder.

81
00:03:11,231 --> 00:03:14,181
So this now lists and copies all my files

82
00:03:14,357 --> 00:03:16,665
over there, including all my dependencies.

83
00:03:17,178 --> 00:03:19,342
So if you have a node_modules folder that

84
00:03:19,342 --> 00:03:21,475
contains a lot of files in there and all of

85
00:03:21,507 --> 00:03:23,895
them are copied and we will need them on the

86
00:03:23,895 --> 00:03:26,733
remote server, but it would be easier if we

87
00:03:26,861 --> 00:03:27,021
would

88
00:03:27,582 --> 00:03:30,420
not copy them because they will actually be

89
00:03:30,788 --> 00:03:32,488
created. All the dependencies will be

90
00:03:32,488 --> 00:03:34,379
installed through our Dockerfile.

91
00:03:34,908 --> 00:03:36,126
So I'll cancel this

92
00:03:37,297 --> 00:03:39,252
and connect to my VPS. And there, if I run

93
00:03:39,445 --> 00:03:40,278
ls, you see

94
00:03:40,839 --> 00:03:43,597
I started copying files. So I will remove

95
00:03:43,869 --> 00:03:46,754
the Dockerfile now with the rm command and

96
00:03:46,754 --> 00:03:47,283
remove

97
00:03:47,957 --> 00:03:49,928
node_modules, the folder, by also adding

98
00:03:50,602 --> 00:03:52,974
-rf. That is the Linux command for removing

99
00:03:53,022 --> 00:03:53,503
a folder.

100
00:03:54,705 --> 00:03:55,731
So I'll do that here

101
00:03:56,597 --> 00:03:58,392
and I'll copy again but without the

102
00:03:58,392 --> 00:04:00,637
node_modules folder. So I'll delete the

103
00:04:00,637 --> 00:04:02,528
node_modules folder on my system here. I

104
00:04:02,528 --> 00:04:04,676
don't wanna copy these dependencies. And

105
00:04:04,676 --> 00:04:07,247
I'll also specify VPS core here as a remote

106
00:04:07,360 --> 00:04:09,862
path name here so that I copy these files

107
00:04:09,862 --> 00:04:11,541
into a subfolder on my VPS.

108
00:04:13,559 --> 00:04:15,770
Now with that, again, we copy all of that.

109
00:04:16,948 --> 00:04:19,223
And now if I list my files here, I have my

110
00:04:19,223 --> 00:04:20,223
VPS folder there.

111
00:04:21,707 --> 00:04:21,998
I can

112
00:04:22,788 --> 00:04:25,256
cd into it. And one thing I'll do here is

113
00:04:25,369 --> 00:04:26,252
I'll remove the

114
00:04:27,200 --> 00:04:29,819
.git folder with rm -rf because that was

115
00:04:29,996 --> 00:04:31,474
also copied and I don't want it here.

116
00:04:32,245 --> 00:04:34,190
But with that, I now got my project over

117
00:04:34,190 --> 00:04:35,106
there on my VPS.

118
00:04:35,752 --> 00:04:37,563
That's one way of getting it over there. As

119
00:04:37,595 --> 00:04:39,423
you saw, it's maybe not the perfect way. We

120
00:04:39,423 --> 00:04:41,699
had to do a couple of things to not copy too

121
00:04:41,699 --> 00:04:44,569
much, but now the project is there on the

122
00:04:44,569 --> 00:04:45,210
VPS.

123
00:04:45,835 --> 00:04:48,688
An alternative to using this

124
00:04:49,602 --> 00:04:51,750
SCP command, which has its issues as

125
00:04:51,846 --> 00:04:52,231
mentioned,

126
00:04:52,808 --> 00:04:55,485
is that you could use the rsync command.

127
00:04:55,950 --> 00:04:58,739
This is a program that may not be installed

128
00:04:58,739 --> 00:05:00,022
on your system though.

129
00:05:00,583 --> 00:05:01,769
On Windows, you

130
00:05:02,346 --> 00:05:05,472
may need to switch to your WSL2 environment

131
00:05:05,472 --> 00:05:07,299
to have it available there or to install it.

132
00:05:08,358 --> 00:05:09,368
But that is a more

133
00:05:09,897 --> 00:05:12,864
versatile copy command that allows you to

134
00:05:12,864 --> 00:05:15,381
specify which paths and folders should be

135
00:05:15,494 --> 00:05:16,841
excluded when copying.

136
00:05:17,578 --> 00:05:20,368
I also just noticed I, for example, copied

137
00:05:20,400 --> 00:05:23,030
my data folder, which contained my SQLite

138
00:05:23,030 --> 00:05:25,548
database from my development server, which I

139
00:05:25,548 --> 00:05:27,264
of course also wouldn't want to have

140
00:05:27,921 --> 00:05:30,070
on my remote server. I wanna have a brand

141
00:05:30,166 --> 00:05:30,856
new database there.

142
00:05:31,449 --> 00:05:33,999
So I will delete the data folder on the VPS.

143
00:05:34,512 --> 00:05:36,762
Another disadvantage of SCP. You have to

144
00:05:36,762 --> 00:05:38,625
clean up stuff you don't want to copy or

145
00:05:38,690 --> 00:05:41,324
delete it before you start copying. rsync

146
00:05:41,324 --> 00:05:43,799
gives you more flexibility. So if that tool

147
00:05:44,136 --> 00:05:44,827
is available—

148
00:05:45,357 --> 00:05:47,044
and don't worry if it's not, we'll have

149
00:05:47,044 --> 00:05:49,341
another alternative thereafter— but if it is

150
00:05:49,550 --> 00:05:52,073
available, you could use rsync for getting

151
00:05:52,105 --> 00:05:53,422
your files onto the VPS.

152
00:05:54,290 --> 00:05:56,812
So on the VPS, to show you rsync, I'll

153
00:05:57,407 --> 00:05:59,817
get out of this folder and I'll remove this

154
00:05:59,817 --> 00:06:00,877
VPS course folder.

155
00:06:01,985 --> 00:06:03,462
And then use rsync here.

156
00:06:04,153 --> 00:06:04,602
And actually,

157
00:06:05,678 --> 00:06:07,653
we can just copy this command here, of

158
00:06:07,685 --> 00:06:09,676
course, and then just fill in the blanks.

159
00:06:10,720 --> 00:06:11,442
rsync

160
00:06:12,245 --> 00:06:15,039
like this. And I wanna exclude node_modules,

161
00:06:15,135 --> 00:06:17,383
I wanna exclude data and so on. But of

162
00:06:17,464 --> 00:06:20,884
course, my target here is just VPS course,

163
00:06:21,012 --> 00:06:23,758
my alias of my remote server I set up in the

164
00:06:23,758 --> 00:06:24,689
SSH config.

165
00:06:27,651 --> 00:06:29,456
Now with that, that was copied. It's also

166
00:06:29,472 --> 00:06:32,034
way quicker, not just because it copies

167
00:06:32,211 --> 00:06:34,468
less, but also because it compresses it

168
00:06:34,484 --> 00:06:36,360
before copying, which is another advantage.

169
00:06:37,710 --> 00:06:39,532
And now I got this folder here,

170
00:06:42,929 --> 00:06:44,847
and if I cd into that folder,

171
00:06:45,589 --> 00:06:47,603
you see there is no data folder in there, so

172
00:06:47,603 --> 00:06:49,554
it's much cleaner. This is definitely better

173
00:06:49,554 --> 00:06:51,955
than SCP if you have this command available.

174
00:06:52,834 --> 00:06:54,777
The last and maybe best option though, the

175
00:06:54,777 --> 00:06:57,153
most versatile one is to use Git.

176
00:06:57,956 --> 00:07:00,461
If you're managing your project via Git, so

177
00:07:00,461 --> 00:07:04,170
if you're using Git and you're linking it to

178
00:07:04,170 --> 00:07:05,406
a remote repository,

179
00:07:05,985 --> 00:07:09,372
you can clone it onto the VPS. And of course

180
00:07:09,372 --> 00:07:11,781
the project I shared with you is in a public

181
00:07:11,781 --> 00:07:14,350
repository. I pushed it to a public

182
00:07:14,350 --> 00:07:16,421
repository so you can just use that.

183
00:07:17,946 --> 00:07:19,036
And therefore I'll

184
00:07:19,564 --> 00:07:20,558
move out of my folder here,

185
00:07:21,327 --> 00:07:22,112
remove that

186
00:07:22,769 --> 00:07:23,490
demo folder,

187
00:07:24,131 --> 00:07:26,791
and now we can just use git clone. And Git

188
00:07:27,801 --> 00:07:29,548
should be available on the VPS already. You

189
00:07:29,580 --> 00:07:31,599
can try running Git and it should show some

190
00:07:31,663 --> 00:07:32,865
info message like this.

191
00:07:33,746 --> 00:07:35,701
Otherwise you need to install it with apt,

192
00:07:36,133 --> 00:07:38,425
but it should really be available on all

193
00:07:38,617 --> 00:07:40,652
Linux distributions. And then you can just

194
00:07:40,780 --> 00:07:41,293
git clone.

195
00:07:41,854 --> 00:07:43,969
So you can go to that repository I shared,

196
00:07:44,180 --> 00:07:45,582
Again, you find it attached,

197
00:07:47,783 --> 00:07:50,053
copy this HTTPS clone link here

198
00:07:52,130 --> 00:07:52,951
and git clone it

199
00:07:54,142 --> 00:07:55,816
and this will now also download it. And

200
00:07:55,913 --> 00:07:57,718
that's of course the easiest way for getting

201
00:07:57,766 --> 00:07:59,708
it onto your system. It's super easy in this

202
00:07:59,708 --> 00:08:01,229
case where I already published it

203
00:08:01,828 --> 00:08:04,481
for you. If that were your own project, you

204
00:08:04,546 --> 00:08:06,744
would have to create your own repository and

