00:08:07,146 --> 00:08:09,478
clone it from there. If it's a private

206
00:08:09,478 --> 00:08:12,421
repository, you will need a deploy key and

207
00:08:12,678 --> 00:08:13,740
you find detailed instructions for that in

208
00:08:13,740 --> 00:08:14,029
the next lecture.

209
00:08:16,030 --> 00:08:18,920
How you could clone a private repository

210
00:08:19,016 --> 00:08:21,265
onto your VPS because many of your projects

211
00:08:21,265 --> 00:08:23,127
may of course be in such a private

212
00:08:23,127 --> 00:08:23,689
repository.

213
00:08:24,332 --> 00:08:26,114
But it's still worth knowing about the other

214
00:08:26,194 --> 00:08:28,073
approaches too because if you just need to

215
00:08:28,089 --> 00:08:29,743
quickly get some file onto

216
00:08:30,273 --> 00:08:31,044
your VPS,

217
00:08:31,622 --> 00:08:34,465
SCP or rsync can be great for that. And as

218
00:08:34,465 --> 00:08:36,504
you saw, you can also use them for deploying

219
00:08:36,536 --> 00:08:37,387
entire projects.
